 "review_22_10": "normal and t are both upper bounds, not a bracket: SE_empty contains the query noise, and with SE_seed ~ 0 (REES46, Sber) the null t has SD ~ 0.68 (design.rehearse); only Tinkoff (seed share 0.89) is near the t reference. normal_scaled / t_scaled use share = se_empty^2 / se^2 per column. The outcome rule (normal, t) is unchanged. Poisson-binomial assumes 22 independent candidates; within a dataset t_loo share the denominator, so the spread is larger and q95 understated.",
